# EvoMan Generalist Agent Evolution

This project investigates the evolution of generalist neural-network-controlled agents in the [EvoMan framework](https://github.com/karinemiras/evoman_framework).

Unlike Task 1, where agents were trained against individual enemies, this task focuses on evolving agents that can perform well across multiple enemies.

Two Genetic Algorithms are compared using the same evolutionary operators but different fitness functions.

## Objective

The goal is to evolve generalist agents using groups of EvoMan enemies and evaluate how well the agents generalize across different opponents.

Two Genetic Algorithms are compared:

- **GA1** – uses EvoMan's default fitness function.
- **GA2** – uses a custom fitness function with a stronger time penalty.

## Algorithms

### GA1

GA1 evaluates each individual against every enemy in the training group and uses the average of the default EvoMan fitness values.

### GA2

GA2 uses the custom fitness function:

```text
fitness = 100 - enemy_energy - 0.05 * time_alive
